## AI action log (`../ai_#N.log`)

- Global enable flag `DAT_01027180` (byte, never written by game code — developer switch); `DAT_01027181` = no flush.
  Enabled by `src/patches/AiLogs.cpp`.
- At map start `FUN_00B610B0(mapName)` (called from `0x007E0AD6` and `0x008099C9`) opens the 8 slots only if the flag
  is set; existing files are deleted first.
- Row writer gate `FUN_00B610E0`: flag set, player at `[this+0x70]` is AI (player vtable `+0x18C`), slot = player
  number (vtable `+0x2C`) - 1.
- 8 per-player log slots at `0x010271A8 + 0x24 * n`, initialised by `FUN_00B60340` (file `../ai_#%i.log`, relative to `bin`).
- Writer `FUN_00B603F0`: CSV-like rows `Action, Object, ObjInfo, Value, Money, <7 resources>, Heroes, Towns`.
- Check `FUN_00B60320` returns the flag (used e.g. by market trading logs).

## Data parameters — `RPGStats/AI/Adventure` in `GameMechanics/RPGStats/DefaultStats.xdb`

Type registered by `FUN_009511A0`. Overridden by H5X in `data/h5x-core.pak`.

- Per difficulty (`DifficultyEasy/Normal/Hard/Heroic`): `AttackHumanAggressivityCoef`, `AttackComputerAggressivityCoef`,
  `CowardiceVersusHuman/Computer`, `RolesSearchNear/FarMaxCost`, `ArmyPowerCoefBonusPerHeroLevel`, `ValueOfTown`,
  `AvengerVersusHuman/ComputerCoef`, `TownBuildPeriodInDays`, `CheckTownsInDanger`, `CheckHeroesDanger`,
  `ConsiderGarrisoningHeroToImportantTown`, `HireHeroesBase/PerTown/GlobalLimit`, `GrailSearch*`, `Threats*`,
  `StrategicCaptureDistance`, `TownCreatureGrowthCoef`.
- Global: `Search*` (destination search), `Roles*` (hero roles Commander / Collector / Supplier / Freelancer),
  `SupplyDayIncomes`, `Creature*Coef` (army strength estimate), ~30 `ValueOf*`, `Siege*`, `CollectPathBonuses*`,
  `Necromancy_*`.
- H5X vs ToE (as of this survey, set on purpose to push the AI toward exploring instead of rushing — see
  "Problems to fix"): aggressivity 1 → 0.5, cowardice → 0.3, `AvengerVersusComputerCoef` → 0,
  most `CreatureOver*` / luck / morale coefs → 0.000001, `ValueOfTown` ×4, threat parameters raised.

Combat AI parameters are in the sibling section `RPGStats/AI/Combat`.
